<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The launcher icon's foreground layer: "Solid Wedge", the candidate the owner chose out of six.

  THIS FILE IS A TRANSCRIPTION, NOT A DRAWING. Every number below is read off
  docs/design/icon-candidates/solid-wedge.svg, which is the source of truth, and
  android/gate/appicon_test.go parses both files and compares the geometry it evaluates from
  each. Do not adjust a coordinate here. Adjust the candidate, and let the gate require this
  file to follow; a number changed only here is a second design nobody approved, and it is
  invisible in review because both files look right on their own.

  WHY THIS MARK. The product is a terminal multi-agent tracker. The zigzag is the prompt's
  reversal carried at the heaviest weight the set allows, so what survives downscaling is mass
  rather than detail, and the cursor is the one filled shape, which is what keeps it reading as a
  cursor beside a stroked letter without needing a gap to separate them. Butt caps cut both
  terminals flat at the diagonal's own angle and mitred joins give the reversals real points:
  both are stated explicitly below rather than left to the platform default, because a default
  that agrees with the specification today is still not the specification.

  WHY IT IS A VECTOR AND WHY THERE ARE NO PNG BUCKETS. minSdk is 33 and adaptive icons landed
  at 26, so mipmap-anydpi-v26 resolves on every device this app supports; a density ladder of
  rasterised copies would be twelve files that can disagree with each other and with this one.

  GEOMETRY. The canvas is the adaptive 108x108dp and the mark sits at the candidate's own
  coordinates, neither scaled nor translated. Measured from rendered pixels at 10x, the drawn
  extent spans x 24.95..79.95 and y 32.35..76.15, and the furthest point from the centre is the
  cursor bar's bottom-right corner at (80, 76.25), r = 34.2. THAT IS 1.2 PAST the 33dp circle
  Android guarantees against every launcher mask. It clears the masks in practice (a 72dp circle
  reaches 36, and the corner sits well inside a 72dp squircle's rounding), and this file
  reproduces the approved drawing rather than quietly re-centring it, but the overrun is real and
  is filed as agents-tracker-aww2 for the owner to accept or close. Re-measure from pixels if the
  artwork ever moves: the arithmetic that ignores what a mitred join does past the end of its own
  path understates every corner, which is how the candidate's comment came to carry 32.5.

  COLOUR IS A TOKEN, NOT A VALUE. [p-hero] is the mark's colour in the candidate and
  swarm_hero is what it is called here, joined through android/design-tokens.tsv (PB-TOK-1). An
  icon-only literal would be a colour that entered the product without passing through that
  origin, which is precisely what the token gate exists to refuse. The token names carry a
  leading double hyphen; it is spelled [p-hero] here because XML forbids that sequence inside a
  comment.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108"
    android:viewportHeight="108">

    <!-- The zigzag: three legs, one open channel between them at 48dp. -->
    <path
        android:pathData="M57,36 L34,48 L57,60 L34,72"
        android:strokeColor="@color/swarm_hero"
        android:strokeWidth="8.5"
        android:strokeLineCap="butt"
        android:strokeLineJoin="miter" />

    <!-- The cursor: one straight bar on the zigzag's own baseline, and the only filled shape. -->
    <path
        android:pathData="M62,67.75 L80,67.75 L80,76.25 L62,76.25 Z"
        android:fillColor="@color/swarm_hero" />
</vector>
